<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Krnov</h1><p class="st-meta">1377 CE – 1918 CE (approx.) · capital Krnov</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Silesian duchy, known in German as Jägerndorf, held successively by Přemyslids, Hohenzollerns and the princes of Liechtenstein.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krnov">Krnov</a> (Jägerndorf) emerged from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/premyslid-dynasty">Přemyslid</a> lands of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-opava">Duchy of Opava</a>. After Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicholas-ii">Nicholas II</a> died in 1365 his sons divided his possessions, and by 1377 John I held Krnov together with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raciborz">Racibórz</a> as his own duchy, a fief of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bohemia">Kingdom of Bohemia</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>After several changes of ruler, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krnov">Krnov</a> was bought in 1523 by Margrave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-the-pious">George of Brandenburg-Ansbach</a>, who introduced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lutheranism">Lutheranism</a> and rebuilt the castle. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-hohenzollern">Hohenzollern</a> heirs held it until 1621, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-george-duke-of-jagerndorf">Johann Georg</a> lost it for supporting the Bohemian revolt. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-ii-holy-roman-emperor">Emperor Ferdinand II</a> then granted it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karl-i-prince-of-liechtenstein">Karl of Liechtenstein</a>, whose family kept the ducal title thereafter.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-the-great">Frederick II of Prussia</a> cited the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-hohenzollern">Hohenzollern</a> claim to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krnov">Krnov</a> when he invaded <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-silesia">Silesia</a>, and in 1742 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> annexed the northern part, while the town stayed in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-upper-and-lower-silesia">Austrian Silesia</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-liechtenstein">Liechtensteins</a> kept the title until 1918, when Krnov became part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-krnov.jpg" alt="Duchy of Krnov" width="320" height="184"><figcaption>Image: Simplicius; derivative work by Blahma · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ducatus_Troppaviensis_(Blaeu_1645_-_Silesia_Ducatus).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1377 CE – 1918 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Krnov</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>John I of Opava-Racibórz, George of Brandenburg-Ansbach, Karl of Liechtenstein</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism, Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German, Czech</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/czech-republic">Czech Republic</a>, <a href="/countries/poland">Poland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Duchy of Jägerndorf</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1648&amp;focus=duchy-of-krnov" aria-label="Duchy of Krnov on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5085 436 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Krnov lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5405 692L5410 696M5405 692L5330 692M5405 692L5282 625"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5410 696h0M5330 692h0M5282 625h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5405 692h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5405 692h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Krnov. <a href="/atlas?year=1648&amp;focus=duchy-of-krnov">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
